All that Cartman have is innocent fun, Kyle.

953
00:41:23,300 --> 00:41:25,780
Anyway, Cartman obeys, and off they go with Kenny's ashes.

954
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:27,179
Oh, and would you look at that?

955
00:41:30,500 --> 00:41:31,579
Cartman was right.

956
00:41:31,699 --> 00:41:33,460
The McCormicks do have a robot guard.

957
00:41:33,739 --> 00:41:36,280
How and with what money, though, is anyone's guess.

958
00:41:36,519 --> 00:41:39,960
Anyway, the rest of the episode is whack as they try to get that lost ticket stub back,

959
00:41:40,159 --> 00:41:41,519
but you can check it out for yourself sometime.

960
00:41:41,840 --> 00:41:45,719
Let's rather look at one of the most famous Cartman was right scenes in the history of the show,

961
00:41:45,960 --> 00:41:48,800
and ask ourselves, was he actually right?

962
00:41:49,280 --> 00:41:53,739
In two days before the day after tomorrow, Stan and Cartman crash a boat into a beaver dam,

963
00:41:53,940 --> 00:41:57,920
causing a massive flood in the town of Beaverton, and I'm-I'm talking massive, dude.

964
00:41:58,420 --> 00:42:04,219
Earlier today, a break in the beaver dam, which broke open, trapping people in their houses and destroying their lives.

965
