Yeah, okay, that number is grossly over-exaggerated, but it's still pretty bad.

969
00:42:18,039 --> 00:42:23,349
False reports immediately start spreading, claiming that the trapped Beavertonians have already resorted to cannibalism.

970
00:42:23,659 --> 00:42:27,420
Stan is absolutely horrified and ridden with guilt, but Cartman is, of course, just being himself.

971
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:29,380
You saw those people trapped on the roofs?

972
00:42:29,559 --> 00:42:30,440
Yeah, that was pretty funny.

973
00:42:30,699 --> 00:42:31,199
Pretty funny?

974
00:42:31,579 --> 00:42:32,480
Dude, we did that!

975
00:42:32,639 --> 00:42:33,559
Hey, hey, no, dawg.

976
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:37,239
We aren't the ones who built a town beneath a giant beaver dam, okay?

977
00:42:37,380 --> 00:42:39,000
But they're trapped now, and nobody's helping them.

978
00:42:39,269 --> 00:42:40,760
Well, they should've gotten out of there.

979
00:42:41,380 --> 00:42:44,469
Cartman goes on victim-blaming and refusing to take any accountability whatsoever,

980
00:42:44,860 --> 00:42:48,159
because that might probably cause him to spontaneously combust or something.

981
00:42:48,420 --> 00:42:52,400
Oh, and he somehow finds an opportunity during all of this to throw around his anti-Semitism, too.

982
00:42:52,579 --> 00:42:53,539
I know what you're thinking, Stan.

983
00:42:54,119 --> 00:42:56,800
You're thinking you're gonna go tell Kyle, but Kyle is a Jew rat.

984
00:42:57,059 --> 00:42:59,619
He has his Jew ethics while he hoards his greedy Jew gold,

985
00:42:59,659 --> 00:43:01,460
and he will Jew you out if you tell him about this!

986
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:06,019
Times like these that I personally like to picture Cartman walking around with a muzzle strapped with that giant yap of his.

987
00:43:06,139 --> 00:43:10,239
Anyway, reports follow that global warming was responsible for the damn break, and Randy, the geologist,

988
00:43:10,340 --> 00:43:10,940
ends up at the state gate.

989
00:43:10,980 --> 00:43:14,380
Capitol building warning government officials of more catastrophic events to come.

990
00:43:14,619 --> 00:43:16,420
Excuse me, sir, but when?

991
00:43:16,780 --> 00:43:20,820
My colleagues in the scientific community are still running tests, but day after tomorrow.

992
00:43:21,940 --> 00:43:23,039
Oh! Peace and carry!

993
00:43:23,519 --> 00:43:23,980
Peace and carry!

994
00:43:24,239 --> 00:43:24,519
Peace and carry!

995
00:43:25,179 --> 00:43:26,360
Yes, like that one movie.

996
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:28,079
Oh, no, sorry, wait.

997
00:43:28,380 --> 00:43:29,659
We finished running the tests!

998
00:43:30,360 --> 00:43:34,780
Global warming is going to strike two days before the day after tomorrow.

999
00:43:35,099 --> 00:43:36,039
Oh my god.

1000
00:43:36,699 --> 00:43:37,420
That's today.

1001
00:43:41,659 --> 00:43:43,780
No! No!

1002
00:43:43,780 --> 00:43:48,320
Cue headless chickens running around the state capital, hysteric townsfolk flooding grocery mart,

1003
00:43:48,460 --> 00:43:52,420
and desperate citizens causing a major traffic jam trying to get the heck out of Dodge.

1004
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:55,539
Those who can't eventually end up locked inside the community center.

1005
00:43:55,780 --> 00:43:58,440
Stan, I never thought global warming could happen so fast.

1006
00:43:58,860 --> 00:43:59,940
It isn't global warming.

1007
00:44:00,079 --> 00:44:01,880
Huh? Global warming isn't happening right now.

1008
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:03,599
It's not what caused the Beaverton flood.

1009
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:04,360
How do you know that?

1010
00:44:04,500 --> 00:44:05,699
I know what did cause the flood.

1011
00:44:05,820 --> 00:44:10,579
Stan ends up telling Kyle exactly what happened, and Kyle says that they had to tell someone immediately, which, yes,

1012
00:44:10,679 --> 00:44:12,119
would absolutely be the right thing to do.

1013
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:14,280
Stan, people in Beaverton are still trapped on their roofs.

1014
00:44:14,699 --> 00:44:16,440
Nobody's helping them because they think they can't go outside.

1015
00:44:16,699 --> 00:44:18,179
If you're so caring, Kyle,

1016
00:44:18,480 --> 00:44:20,860
why don't you share some of your Jew gold with the people caught in the flood?

1017
00:44:21,360 --> 00:44:22,659
There's that Jew gold obsession again.

1018
00:44:23,119 --> 00:44:26,510
Kyle and Stan ignore him and instead try to think of how they can help the people stuck in Beaverton.

1019
00:44:26,960 --> 00:44:28,440
We'd like to be rescued, please.

1020
00:44:29,539 --> 00:44:30,860
Why haven't they come for us?

1021
00:44:31,079 --> 00:44:32,079
I don't know.

1022
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:33,320
Here comes a boat.

1023
